Summary: Fix a zoomed or cropped OpenGL picture after a program changes the display mode
Category: graphics
Kind: fix
Origin: wine-mac-builds
Upstream: candidate (draft in .local/bug-reports/). WineHQ master still
 uses virtual_rect here (checked 2026-11-25).
Why: With EmulateModeset on, win32u creates each window's GL client surface
 "raw" and renders into a framebuffer surface (an FBO of the emulated,
 virtual size) that it blits to the client surface at the monitor's real
 size (monitor_rect). winemac ignored client.raw and set the CGL surface
 backing size to virtual_rect, so after a mode change the blit landed in a
 backing of the wrong size and the picture was zoomed or cropped. winex11
 already uses "raw ? monitor_rect : virtual_rect" for the same thing; do the
 same. Surfaces that aren't raw keep virtual_rect, and while the emulated mode
 matches the screen the two rects have the same size.
 Seen in White Wolf (Gcenx 11.21, our macfixes 11.21 build1): the log
 shows "Using experimental framebuffer OpenGL surface" and the picture
 overflows the window. Wine 10.0 has no framebuffer surface, so this is
 11.x only.
Programs: White Wolf: its OpenGL picture is zoomed and cropped after it
 changes the display mode (Wine 11, EmulateModeset)
Related: winemac-centre-fullscreen-gdi; the GL and GDI halves of a
 fullscreen picture under EmulateModeset
Status: 11.21: 2026-11-16: built in macfixes-11.21-build2; confirmed: White
 Wolf's picture is no longer zoomed (Second Chance integration run).

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
index a67010a..e5e50dc 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
@@ -1149,7 +1149,7 @@ static void macdrv_context_select_drawable(struct macdrv_context *context, struc
     if (drawable && drawable->client)
     {
         struct macdrv_client_surface *surface = impl_from_client_surface(drawable->client);
-        RECT rect = surface->client.virtual_rect;
+        RECT rect = surface->client.raw ? surface->client.monitor_rect : surface->client.virtual_rect;
         macdrv_make_context_current(context->context, surface->cocoa_view, cgrect_from_rect(rect));
         return;
     }
